WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:00.420
JOANNA SMITH: Hi.

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.860
I'm Joanna Smith,
and today, we're

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.818
looking at how to keep
your employees connected

00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:04.650
and engaged--

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.952
even when they can't
be in the office.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.910
Co-workers and teams are
able to stay connected

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.800
while working remotely
thanks to tools

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.560
like collaborative documents,
video meetings, and team chat

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.400
rooms.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.260
On a larger scale,
enabling employees

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.770
to feel connected across teams
and to the company as a whole

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.120
can be a challenge.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.890
One tactic that's
especially effective

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:25.580
here is to host a
virtual all-hands.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.630
An all-hands meeting is
unique in its ability

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.400
to bring an
organization together

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.830
while ensuring that everyone
receives the same information.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.310
In fact, a recent
study by igloo Software

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:39.000
found that 75% of remote
workers believe they miss out

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.840
on important information.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.450
This can cause
operational issues,

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.030
and result in a
disengaged workforce.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.730
But the logistics of running
an all-hands meeting remotely

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.470
may seem daunting.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.630
Fortunately, you can
use G Suite and Google

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.480
Meet the host a virtual
all-hands for up to 100,000

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.040
employees, whether
they're working

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.890
from their home, office,
on the factory floor,

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.350
or out in the field.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.350
Google Meet is our
enterprise-grade video

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.860
conferencing solution that takes
advantage of Google Cloud's

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.990
secure-by-design
infrastructure, and features

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.330
a number of proactive
counter-abuse protections

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:12.408
to help protect your data
and safeguard your privacy.

00:01:12.408 --> 00:01:13.950
With Google Meet,
your video meetings

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.890
are secure, easy to join,
and offer helpful features,

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.480
like adaptive
layouts, so that you

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.810
can focus on what matters most.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.820
Best of all, with G Suite, you
get so much more than meetings.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.260
You can schedule
and join meetings

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.600
directly from Gmail
or Google Calendar,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.150
easily present your screen
or collaborate on a document

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.550
during the meeting, and
securely record a meeting

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.400
and have it saved to Google
Drive to be shared later.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.900
These same features
that make Google

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.475
Meet so effective as a
video conferencing solution

00:01:39.475 --> 00:01:41.600
are what make it simple
and straightforward to host

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.540
a virtual all-hands meeting.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.333
So let's take a look at how
that might come together.

00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:48.000
First, we'll need to
create the calendar

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.522
event for our all-hands.

00:01:49.522 --> 00:01:51.480
We'll select the time,
and then we can fill out

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.980
the initial
information, including

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.070
the event title and any details
we need in the description.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.950
Then we need to add Google
Meet video conferencing, which

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.980
is as simple as a click.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.660
Our all-hands is also going
to offer a livestream,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.240
so to enable that, we'll want
to switch to the Event Details

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.257
page.

00:02:07.257 --> 00:02:09.840
The option to add a livestream
is nested under the Google Meet

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.290
additional details view, and
all it takes is a single click.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.720
Now, we can invite our
co-presenters and attendees,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.440
and just like that, our virtual
all-hands has been scheduled.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.330
A single Google Meet
video conference

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:25.500
supports up to 250 participants,
while a livestream supports up

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.540
to 100,000 viewers.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.060
Depending on the size and
nature of your all-hands,

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.430
you may want to create
two separate events--

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.250
one that contains the Google
Video conference, to which you

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.890
only invite presenters,
and then a second event

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.280
for the view-only livestream,
where you can invite attendees.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.530
Creating a view-only
event is a simple edit

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.060
on the initial event.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.670
From the event details dialog,
click the three-dot menu

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.573
button, and select
Create View Only Event.

00:02:50.573 --> 00:02:51.990
You can then invite
your attendees

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.790
and even modify the
event description,

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.248
if there is separate information
to share for the audience.

00:02:58.802 --> 00:03:00.260
On the day of the
event, we'll want

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.172
to be sure that
everyone can join,

00:03:02.172 --> 00:03:04.130
whether they're using
shared video conferencing

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.410
devices, the Google
Meet mobile app,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.150
or watching the
view-only livestream

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.853
from any modern browser.

00:03:09.853 --> 00:03:11.270
As the event
organizer, we'll want

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:15.080
to join early so that we can
turn on each of these features.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.970
The livestream doesn't
begin automatically,

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:18.380
and needs to be started.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.270
This allows organizers
to get set up

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.910
and test their presentations
without an accidental audience.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.370
When everyone is ready,
we'll click Start Streaming.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.950
We'll know the
livestream is active

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.162
based on the Live tag in
the corner of the screen.

00:03:31.162 --> 00:03:32.870
If we want to make
this virtual all-hands

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.760
available after
the event, we can

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.530
choose to record the meeting.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.290
To begin recording, select the
three dots in the bottom corner

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.780
to open a menu of
additional options.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.490
There, we can click
Record Meeting,

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.280
and another red tag has
appeared in the upper corner,

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.223
to indicate that this
meeting is being recorded.

00:03:49.223 --> 00:03:51.140
The recording will be
emailed to the organizer

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.520
after the livestream ends and
saved securely to Google Drive,

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.340
where can later be distributed
for on-demand viewing.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.360
To stop recording
or streaming, simply

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.400
return to the Options menu.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.040
Also, from this menu, we
can turn on live captions

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.160
to make the meeting
more inclusive.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.840
Live captions and Google Meet
are powered by Google's speech

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.880
recognition
technology, not typed

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.220
by a human, which
helps ensure no one

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.160
outside your organization
is viewing private content.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.779
During the all-hands,
each presenter

00:04:17.779 --> 00:04:21.230
can easily participate, even if
they aren't in the same place.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.730
When it's our turn
to present, we're

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.060
given the option to
share our entire screen,

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.680
a specific window, or
even a single Chrome

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.020
tab, which makes it easy to play
high-quality videos with audio.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.820
And when we're done, we
simply stop presenting.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.260
With these options,
Meet makes it

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.890
easy to have control of the
content you'd like to share.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.080
With distributed teams,
it's especially important

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.890
to have a mechanism in
place for giving feedback.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:47.630
After the all-hands ends, we'll
use Google Forms to quickly

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.400
create a simple survey.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.190
We can customize the format,
randomize the questions,

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.278
and designate certain
questions as required,

00:04:54.278 --> 00:04:55.820
so employees can
share their thoughts

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.500
on the event and content.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.930
Because of the deep
integrations built into G Suite,

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.610
the survey responses
automatically

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.410
populate into a
Google Sheet where

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:06.170
we can view the raw responses,
or use the Explore feature

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:10.190
to get suggestions on pivot
tables or data visualizations.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.230
The feedback form, along
with the recording,

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.360
presented slides,
and follow materials

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.850
can be shared across the
company using an internal portal

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.890
created with Google Sites.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.110
This internal site provides
a quick and easy way

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.910
to keep everyone
on the same page,

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.910
and serves as an on-demand
reference for their content.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.500
A site like this is
especially helpful

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.270
when onboarding new employees,
and it's easy to update,

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.000
so you can keep adding
additional content

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.080
as it becomes available.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.530
And that is how you can
use G Suite and Google Meet

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.320
to host a virtual all-hands to
keep your employees connected

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.740
and engaged, even when they
can't be in the office.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.360
If you aren't
already on G Suite,

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.270
we have a new way to help
you get started immediately.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.460
With our new G Suite
Essentials offering,

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.020
teams and
organizations can start

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.550
collaborating using
the tools you've

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:56.150
seen here in hours, not weeks.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:58.430
G Suite Essentials
includes Google Meet,

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:02.360
Drive, Docs, Sheets,
Slides, Forms, and Sites.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.950
It's compatible with your
existing IT environment,

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:09.140
and there is no need to adopt
a new email or calendar system.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.870
From now through September
30, teams and organizations

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.365
can use G Suite
Essentials at no cost,

00:06:14.365 --> 00:06:15.740
including advanced
functionality,

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.860
like shared Drives,
meeting recordings,

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:19.850
and in-domain live streaming.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.590
For existing G Suite
customers, we're

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:24.920
also enabling access to advanced
Meet functionality at no cost

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.570
through September 30.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.160
This includes
in-domain livestreaming

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.350
for up to 100,000
people, the ability

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.690
to record meetings to
Drive, and larger meetings

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.670
for up to 250 people per call.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:41.690
To learn more about G Suite,
visit gsuite.google.com.

